# ROOT files
*.root

# macOS system files
.DS_Store
._*

# Editor / transient backups
# (restored 2026-08-17: dropping this rule let
#  crabConfig/config_CPV2017UL_MC.yaml.bk get committed as the ONLY copy
#  of the 73-dataset production config -- under a name no loader reads.)
*.bk*

# Others
**/__pycache__/
FrameworkJobReport.xml
*.swp
crab.log
campaign_*

# preflight logs (--preflight, read-only checker output)
preflight_*.log

# CRAB submit/status transcripts and local test scratch (regenerable).
#
# !! NEVER COMMIT A CRAB SUBMISSION TRANSCRIPT. !!
# `crab submit` prints the pre-signed S3 POST policy + signature it uses to
# upload the task sandbox to crabcache_prod. A transcript therefore embeds a
# live credential, and it is huge (submit_UL18_full_20260727_1120.log was
# 1.52 MB / 16,715 lines). One was committed to this PUBLIC repo on 2026-07-27
# (commit 33e3030) before these rules existed; it is gone from HEAD but still
# reachable in history. That particular policy expired 2026-07-27T10:23:37Z,
# so there is nothing to rotate -- but see docs/05_troubleshooting.md A17 and
# docs/03_DECISIONS.md D-2026-08-17-no-logs-in-git before adding any .log.
#
# NB: script/das_ul18_scan_*.log is deliberately NOT ignored -- it is the INPUT
# that script/build_ul18_from_log.py parses, i.e. provenance for the generated
# UL18 configs, and it contains only DAS query output (no credentials).
# Only outputs are ignored here.
submit_*_20*.log
crab_status_*_20*.log
localcheck_*/
local_test_*.log
crab_args.txt
submit_*.log
crab_status_*.log
